    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Alexander states model satisfaction of the scheme; the target uses provability of its instances in the system whose inconsistency is at issue. It borrows the form of Alexander's scheme, not a claim that his model satisfies known factivity."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The target matches the advertised fixed-F, sentence-by-sentence claim: with factivity, known factivity, and the other stated hypotheses, the scheme implies that the system proves falsehood. It is not a direct formalization of the single-sentence SSMT theorem in EA_T."
